WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:08.900
QueryProof reviews SQL against an explicit metric definition. This is the real local application, using fictional commerce data.

2
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:17.009
The query reports 1,110 USD. The independent row calculation gives 400 USD. These values were calculated from this snapshot.

3
00:00:17.009 --> 00:00:26.065
Three orders contribute more than once. Each finding includes the contract clause, a reproducible diagnostic query, and bounded example rows.

4
00:00:26.065 --> 00:00:35.536
Inspect the original and proposed SQL side by side. This deterministic suggestion preserves the metric definition; it has not been accepted.

5
00:00:35.536 --> 00:00:44.030
The revision executes against the same snapshot. Its total is 400 USD, all checks pass, and the intended population is preserved.

6
00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:53.051
Only a checked revision can be accepted. The original review remains in history. Passing is conditional on this contract and snapshot.

7
00:00:53.051 --> 00:01:02.049
Export a readable HTML report or JSON evidence packet. Raw input rows are excluded; finding examples require an explicit choice.

8
00:01:02.049 --> 00:01:20.680
Saved reviews retain their SQL, contract, snapshot identity, and findings. Optional live-model assistance is separate from deterministic evidence.
